WEBVTT

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:16.290
Ms. Selma...

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:18.330
We're hungry!

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:21.540
Yes, yes. It's ready now.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.000
Yay!

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.700
What are we eating today?

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:26.500
Today is...

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:30.040
Great work today as always, everyone!

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.330
Li Ling, are you slacking off?

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:34.540
No I'm not!

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:39.000
It's time. You can close the front door now.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.700
Yes, sister.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.000
"Episode 12"
"The Beginning of a New Era, with the Slimes"

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.040
They're not coming back.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:10.700
No...

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:11.830
Mr. Ryoma...

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:13.330
Yes?

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:15.830
I guess we're going to
go our separate ways soon.

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:20.750
Wh-What in the world
am I supposed to say to that?

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:23.950
I'm so unaccustomed to
these types of situations...

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:27.330
Um... Uh...

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:30.250
I remember reading a novel
that had a similar situation.

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:33.830
What did the main character say then...?

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:36.790
Uhh... Uhh...

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:41.040
Right! "It's not like we're never
going to see each other again"!

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:42.830
U-Um, it's not like, uh...

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:45.830
It's not like you're never going to
see each other again, Elia.

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:47.660
She beat me to it!

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:49.450
Right, Ryoma?

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:51.750
Yes! Exactly!

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:57.330
I suppose so... Yes!
We will see each other again!

00:01:57.330 --> 00:02:02.410
Mr. Ryoma, please write to me. I will for sure!

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:04.450
Of course I will!

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:07.040
You idiot!

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:09.000
Wh-What?!

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.000
Be a man! Go for a hug, at the very least!

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.620
What are you talking about, Mr. Hughes?!

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:16.910
You're the lady's guard!

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:20.120
You're supposed to be the one
stopping that type of thing!

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:22.160
I always support what I enjoy watching!

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:23.040
What...

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:29.830
There's no need to be so serious,
he's just an 11-year-old child.

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:36.160
Why does it seem like Mr. Reinhart
is the only one who is really angry...?

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:37.500
Ryoma!

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:43.000
Come on! Be a man, go for it, like this!

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.870
The longer you wait,
the more embarrassing it'll get!

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:46.870
Right?

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:52.950
You totally asked for that.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:54.950
So insensitive.

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:56.500
As always.

00:02:56.500 --> 00:03:01.080
Please don't tease.
The lady must be very uncomfortable...

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:04.790
What kind of reaction is that?!

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:09.080
So scary!

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:15.910
They're back!

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:21.540
The nightmare limour bird...

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:24.080
Is it cautious of me?

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:26.000
Mr. Reinhart.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.790
I'll step away for a little.

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:28.870
Why?

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:35.450
That previous interaction might have made
the nightmare limour bird cautious of me.

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:37.250
If I stay, I might interfere.

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.790
I don't care!

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:45.290
I'll never treat your presence
near me as an excuse for my failure.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:52.330
Please stay there,
and watch me tame those birds.

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:55.450
Your presence gives me courage.

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:59.160
I understand. Good luck.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:00.660
Right!

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:52.500
My lady, the contract! The taming contract!

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:54.700
Oh, right!

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:09.080
I did it!

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:10.250
You did it!

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:11.830
You did great!

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:13.660
Well done, Elia!

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:15.290
Score!

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:17.580
She got nine birds at once?!

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:19.080
Congratulations!

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:20.120
You did it!

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:22.120
It is truly wonderful!

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:24.620
You did it, my lady!

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:29.080
Thank you very much! So many pretty birds!

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:32.580
Right... Now it's my turn!

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:36.830
You're going to try, too!

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:41.120
I'm not as good as you, but I'll see
if I can get a share of your luck.

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:46.660
It's similar to a violin, but I've never
seen that instrument before.

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:48.250
Good luck, Ryoma.

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:51.870
What will his performance sound like?
I'm excited to hear it!

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:53.870
Good luck!

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:55.040
Yes!

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:36.660
I've never heard that tune before.

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:38.500
The scale he's playing in is quite rare.

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:42.080
It's very comforting for some reason.

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:44.870
Why are you crying?

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:46.870
I have no idea...

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:02.370
What?!

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:04.120
So many?!

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:10.450
You...

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:13.040
I thought you were cautious of me.

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:17.750
Mr. Ryoma! The contract! The contract!

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:19.580
Oh, right!

00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:30.410
Contract... complete...

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:35.540
Hey, you...

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:44.660
Congratulations, Mr. Ryoma!

00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:46.580
Great!

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:48.330
Impressive.

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:50.620
Seriously awesome!

00:08:50.620 --> 00:08:52.660
Good job!

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:55.700
That was a great experience.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:59.040
Taming a limour bird, huh?

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:01.660
I wish we could share in his luck.

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:04.830
I'm glad you both succeeded, Elia, Ryoma.

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:07.080
Congratulations, Mr. Ryoma!

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:10.910
Taming a limour bird is very difficult.

00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:16.660
Taming multiple at once,
that's incredibly impressive, both of you!

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:17.910
My lady.

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:19.000
Yes?

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:22.290
Could you perform
a monster appraisal on this bird?

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:23.580
Yes!

00:09:28.450 --> 00:09:29.750
What?

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:31.120
What's wrong?

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:34.000
This one! This one is an advanced species, too!

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:35.330
What?!

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:38.000
Its color is different from mine.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:43.540
Oh, it's not a nightmare,
it's a "phantom limour bird," apparently.

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:47.250
It can cast light magic, not dark magic!

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:49.330
There's a species like that?!

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:51.000
Light magic...

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:52.540
Incredible...

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:57.200
The phantom is even more rare
than the nightmare.

00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:02.620
I never thought I'd be able to see
both at once during my lifetime.

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:12.370
He did mention that he isn't compatible
with bird-type monsters,

00:10:12.370 --> 00:10:15.290
but I didn't think he would get
a warning just by getting close...

00:10:16.660 --> 00:10:18.370
A new mode of transportation!

00:10:18.370 --> 00:10:20.160
A little too conspicuous, though...

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:26.000
Yes, please take me to Mr. Ryoma!

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:33.700
That night, a huge banquet was held.

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:39.660
It was both a celebration of the lady
successfully taming the limour birds,

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:43.080
and a farewell party to me.

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:06.950
Yes, my travels with
the lady and her family are...

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:09.870
...almost...

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:21.580
The party is still going strong.

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:24.660
I wonder if they're going to
keep going all night.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:27.450
I hope nobody gets a hangover.

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:30.910
Yes, since you're leaving tomorrow morning.

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:32.250
Yes...

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:50.040
Mr. Ryoma, you'll be living
near the mines from tomorrow, right?

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:55.750
Yes. If I'm going to patrol there frequently,
I might as well live there.

00:11:55.750 --> 00:11:59.910
I can also train magic there
without bothering anyone.

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:03.750
I'll build some rooms over time.

00:12:03.750 --> 00:12:05.580
I see...

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:14.620
My lady, you're going to enter
the school dormitories, right?

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:26.040
Children of nobles are supposed to go to
the school in the capital from age 12.

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:28.200
There's no law or anything...

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:35.580
But it just looks bad unless
there is a special reason.

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:37.290
I see.

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:39.160
Also...

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:44.250
Also?

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:48.080
I don't have anyone
close enough to call a friend.

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:58.500
Most people are afraid of either
my status or my magical power.

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:01.160
Status aside...

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:06.000
You do indeed hold a huge
amount of magical power,

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:11.250
but is that really enough to
scare people away like that?

00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:15.410
I made a mistake a while ago.

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:18.870
When I was five years old,

00:13:18.870 --> 00:13:25.330
an older boy visited my house
and offered to teach me magic.

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:34.870
I couldn't control the magic well,
and ended up freezing the boy.

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:39.000
Of course, we unfroze him immediately.

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:43.000
He was fine, and his family forgave us, but...

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:44.370
But?

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:59.120
It seems like that boy said that I did it
on purpose, or I attack those who cross me.

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:05.120
Exaggerated rumors spread
amongst the nobles,

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:09.080
which scared people off.

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:12.830
That's... quite terrible.

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:17.540
But it's true that I made a mistake.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:23.410
I can't deny that, but... um...

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:25.040
Mr. Ryoma, are you...

00:14:26.830 --> 00:14:28.620
...um...

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:32.790
...all right?

00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:40.250
I mean, hearing that,
are you afraid of me, or...

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:43.660
Oh, of course I'm fine.

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:51.330
It is a fact that I lost control of
my magic and hurt someone.

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:55.790
I wouldn't say you have no blame at all.

00:14:55.790 --> 00:15:02.250
But that type of thing is bound to happen
once or twice to anyone.

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:06.040
Mr. Ryoma?

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:09.370
I mean, um, please rest assured.

00:15:09.370 --> 00:15:14.120
No matter what happens,
I will never be afraid of you, my lady!

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:15.950
Thank you.

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:20.620
On the other hand, do you... think I'm...

00:15:20.620 --> 00:15:23.040
Please don't worry.

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:29.700
I won't ever be afraid of
you either, no matter what.

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:36.830
I almost forgot, I wanted you to take something.

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:37.830
Hmm?

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:42.450
What is this?

00:15:42.450 --> 00:15:43.830
Please open it.

00:15:49.750 --> 00:15:51.000
A ruby...?

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:57.410
This is a necklace I received
from my mother on my 10th birthday.

00:15:58.330 --> 00:15:59.500
Magic power...?

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:03.000
You noticed! Impressive as always.

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:04.870
The ruby is a magic stone.

00:16:04.870 --> 00:16:10.200
Doesn't that make this
a very rare and expensive item?

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:11.450
Indeed it does.

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:15.500
Wait, I can't take this then! It's too precious!

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:18.950
I want you to take it.

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:21.950
But no, it's too precious!

00:16:21.950 --> 00:16:26.700
I'm not giving it to you.
I want you to hold on to it.

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:29.540
Hold on?

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:31.750
It's a good luck charm!

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:36.910
Exchanging precious items
with a friend before parting ways

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:43.410
will help you see them again.
It's an old saying.

00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:51.660
This must be very precious to you. Are you sure?

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:54.250
If I wasn't, I wouldn't have brought it up.

00:16:55.750 --> 00:16:59.500
I understand. I will take good care of this.

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:00.910
Yes!

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:07.160
So does that mean I should
hand her something, too...?

00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:09.910
What's precious to me...?

00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:15.250
Money? Furs? No...

00:17:15.250 --> 00:17:16.830
Mr. Ryoma?

00:17:21.410 --> 00:17:26.000
Please take these, my lady.
These are precious to me.

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:30.250
I also think these two
would be very helpful to you.

00:17:32.620 --> 00:17:34.410
I failed somehow!

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:38.700
Um, I'm sorry, I'm just not very used to this...

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:42.500
No, I'm sorry. I just thought it was
very much in character for you.

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:50.080
Thank you for letting me
take your precious familiars.

00:17:50.080 --> 00:17:52.950
I will take good care of them.

00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:54.950
Thank you.

00:17:58.200 --> 00:18:03.620
And thus, the final night with
the lady and the others passed...

00:18:06.660 --> 00:18:08.120
...and morning came.

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:16.160
Ryoma, when you have some
free time, come visit our town.

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:17.870
I'm sure you can travel super quick.

00:18:17.870 --> 00:18:20.910
Yes, I will visit you for sure.

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:23.330
Good luck, my boy.

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:25.500
Stay sharp, Ryoma.

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:29.700
I very much enjoyed the time
I spent with you, Mr. Ryoma.

00:18:29.700 --> 00:18:33.330
I wish you success in your future endeavors.

00:18:33.330 --> 00:18:37.250
Thank you. Mr. Hughes, Mr. Zeph,

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:41.000
Ms. Jill, Ms. Araune, and Ms. Lillian.

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:42.660
Please be well.

00:18:42.660 --> 00:18:45.620
Yeah. Hey, they're waiting.

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:55.540
Stay safe. But I guess given
who you are, you should be fine.

00:18:55.540 --> 00:18:57.250
Yes. You, too, Mr. Camil.

00:18:57.250 --> 00:18:58.500
Yeah.

00:18:58.500 --> 00:19:01.080
Remember to rest occasionally.

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:05.620
Please let us know right away
if you need anything at all.

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:08.620
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:13.910
And like we promised,
you have to write us letters.

00:19:13.910 --> 00:19:18.910
Try to take care of yourself.
And don't hesitate to rely on us.

00:19:18.910 --> 00:19:24.540
Sir Reinhart, Madam Elise,
Sir Reinbach, Mr. Sebas,

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:27.330
thank you so much for everything.

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:30.290
And... my lady.

00:19:37.620 --> 00:19:39.830
Um, Mr. Ryoma.

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:42.830
Yes, what is it, my lady?

00:19:42.830 --> 00:19:44.290
That.

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:45.450
"That"?

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:50.160
I've been wondering for a while,

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:54.950
but is it correct to assume we are friends?

00:19:54.950 --> 00:19:56.370
Yes.

00:19:56.370 --> 00:20:01.620
Then please, don't call me "my lady"
as if we're strangers.

00:20:01.620 --> 00:20:04.370
Please call me "Elia."

00:20:04.370 --> 00:20:07.410
That's what my family and those close to me do.

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:12.750
I see... Yes.

00:20:12.750 --> 00:20:14.950
Um... Elia.

00:20:14.950 --> 00:20:17.660
Yes! Mr. Ryoma!

00:20:17.660 --> 00:20:22.580
No matter whatever happens at school,
I won't let it get me down.

00:20:22.580 --> 00:20:28.370
I'll study hard and improve my magic
by the time we meet again!

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:31.040
Yes, and the same for me, too!

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:35.580
Also, please don't forget our promise
to meet again in three years!

00:20:35.580 --> 00:20:37.660
Of course, I won't forget.

00:20:37.660 --> 00:20:40.700
If you get too caught up in work and forget,

00:20:40.700 --> 00:20:45.410
I will have to remind you by giving you
a taste of my magic training.

00:20:45.410 --> 00:20:49.410
Th-That I would like to avoid...

00:20:49.410 --> 00:20:53.450
I heard that my mother did that in the past

00:20:53.450 --> 00:20:56.540
to remind my father of a promise he forgot.

00:20:56.540 --> 00:20:58.660
I-I see...

00:20:58.660 --> 00:21:01.830
I'm glad Mr. Reinhart survived that...

00:21:02.830 --> 00:21:06.000
I won't say goodbye.

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:08.450
Instead, Mr. Ryoma, I'll see you again.

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:11.330
Yes, Elia. I'll see you again.

00:21:29.370 --> 00:21:30.910
See you!

00:21:34.080 --> 00:21:36.500
See you... again.

00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:42.450
Right... Let's go! No time to waste!

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:56.200
Mr. Ryoma... I will see you again.

00:22:34.870 --> 00:22:39.330
They're really going to miss each other.

00:22:39.330 --> 00:22:40.950
It's only natural.

00:22:40.950 --> 00:22:45.950
They were almost family,
and now they're separate.

00:22:45.950 --> 00:22:50.830
Sometimes you meet people, sometimes you
part ways. Then you meet more people.

00:22:50.830 --> 00:22:53.330
Ryoma will be fine.

00:22:53.330 --> 00:22:57.450
I'm sure he'll meet many more
new friends from now on.

00:22:57.450 --> 00:23:00.160
Yes, I'm sure.

00:23:01.040 --> 00:23:03.830
May Ryoma's future be full of good fortune.

00:23:03.830 --> 00:23:05.870
Good fortune!

00:23:05.870 --> 00:23:08.370
Live your life to the fullest.

00:23:08.370 --> 00:23:12.040
We will continue to watch over you.

00:23:14.080 --> 00:23:16.660
First I'll stop by Bamboo Forest,

00:23:16.660 --> 00:23:18.750
then off to the mines.

00:23:18.750 --> 00:23:22.080
I have to build a place to sleep!

00:23:22.080 --> 00:23:25.120
Elia said she'll work hard.

00:23:25.120 --> 00:23:27.410
I have to work hard, too.

00:23:28.750 --> 00:23:33.450
In order to make my life
a bit different from yesterday.
